ion Timeline\nTest Requirements\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHousing & Dining\nInternational Students\nApplication Requirements\nTuition, Financial Aid, and Other Expenses\nWorking in the US\nImmigration Documentation\nOrientation\nOrientation Schedule\nRequired Pre-enrollment Documentation\nOnboarding Checklist\nStudent Health Program\nCampus Resources\nProspective Student Events\nHome\nAdmissions & Orientation\nOverview\nGraduate programs in Arts, Sciences and Engineering welcome students who are actively engaged with their education and are looking for a challenging environment to expand their knowledge through further study. Our programs emphasize individualized study, which allows students to create an educational experience using Rochester\u2019s unique facilities, nationally ranked faculty, and superb research infrastructure.\nStudent Profiles\nThe University of Rochester offers graduate students the chance to pursue research at the highest level in an environment scaled to the individual. Graduate education is central to the mission of all schools and is an important vehicle for the missions of both research and professional preparation.\nWe\u2019ve highlighted several students on our student profiles page whose experiences embody the philosophy and the opportunities in their education that we offer to our graduate students.\nProfessional Development\nAt Rochester, we believe that graduate education should comprise rigorous academic study, cutting-edge research, and relevant professional development. Whether your education takes you into academia, government, or the private sector, we have extensive resources to assist you in preparing for your career after graduation.\nThe City of Rochester\nSee our City of Rochester page to learn about what our city has to offer. If you are interested in a campus tour or to meet with potential faculty advisors please contact your Graduate Program Coordinator for more information.\nMore Information\nPlease complete our inquiry form to receive additional information about graduate programs in Arts, Sciences and Engineering at the University of Rochester. If you are interested in signing up for a webinar to learn more about the University of Rochester, you can check available dates on our virtual visits page.\nReport a Digital Accessibility Barrier\nGraduate Education and Postdoctoral Affairs\nLocation\nUniversity of Rochester\nGraduate Education and Postdoctoral Affairs\n206 Lattimore Hall\nP.O. Box 270401\nPhone\n(585) 275-4153\nEmail\nASEGEPA@rochester.edu\nResources for\nProspective students\nCurrent students\nParents & families\nFaculty & staff\nAlumni\nSchools & divisions\nSchool of Arts & Sciences\nHajim School of Engineering\nEastman School of Music\nSchool of Medicine & Dentistry\nSchool of Nursing & Health Sciences\nSimon Business School\nWarner School of Education\nLaboratory for Laser Energetics\nLibraries & collections\nUniversity Libraries\nMemorial Art Gallery\nHelpful links\nBlackboard\nContact\nDirectory\nHuman resources\nInformation technology\nMyPath\nmyURHR\nParking & shuttles\nUR Mobile (app)\nEver better\nAccessibility\nEngagement and Enrichment\nGlobal engagement\nNondiscrimination & Title IX\nResearch impact\nStrategic Plan\nVision & Values\nMore URochester\nNews\nEvents\nAthletics\nArts\nFacebook\nYouTube\nX / Twitter\nTikTok\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nThreads\nFollow URochester\nContact us\n(585) 275-2121\nSee maps and directions\nRochester, NY\nSearchSearch\nFeedback\nPrivacy\nCopyright\nEmergency Information\n\u00a9 University of Rochester 1996\u00e2\u0080\u00932026", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.rochester.edu/college/gradstudies/admissions/index.html#main"], ["", "https://rochester.edu/"], ["Apply", "https://rochester.edu/admissions/"], ["Visit", "https://rochester.edu/visit/"], ["Give", "https://rochester.edu/advancement/"], ["School of Arts & Sciences", "https://www.sas.rochester.edu/"], ["Hajim School of Engineering & Applied Sciences", "htt